# L §4.6 step 2 (round 12b): "In a scenario, a scenario row's replace replaces the base's row at the same keys on its
# span whatever the two rows' known dates, the scenario standing above its base"; L §6.4 "a stipulation of the base
# known on the scenario's own known day is replaced too". The base's v2 (known 2026-11-01) is known after the
# scenario's row (2026-10-20): in the scenario salary is 0 PLN from 2027 (s1), the base's 5 000 before (s2); the base
# reads v2 (b).
=== hh.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-11-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input salary: money PLN

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  salary = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-11-01
  replace salary = 6 000.00 PLN "aneks"

ask b: salary law 2027-06-30
=== stop.tally
scenario stop over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version stop_salary
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace salary = 0 PLN "założenie"

ask s1: salary in stop law 2027-06-30
ask s2: salary in stop law 2026-06-30
=== expect
b: 6 000.00 PLN
  held: salary = 6 000.00 PLN (v2), read for 2027-06-30
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2026-11-15
s1: 0.00 PLN
  world: stop
  held: salary = 0.00 PLN (stop_salary), read for 2027-06-30
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2026-11-15
s2: 5 000.00 PLN
  world: stop
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-11-15
